Corresponding source: https://github.com/inteliboy/rustdesk-api-server/tree/main/webclient
(the built files are produced from it with `npm ci && npm run build`).

ORIGIN
------
The client is taken from CortenDesk's web client (webclient/ in
https://github.com/Vaso73/cortendesk, version 1.9.1, commit 5d5470f), AGPL-3.0-only,
"a from-scratch TypeScript implementation of the RustDesk wire protocol".
Only its webclient/ folder and its licence text were used; nothing else of
CortenDesk (in particular not its console, and not the "Attex" admin theme it
bundles under a separate licence) is part of this repository.

The RustDesk protocol definitions in protos/ come from the RustDesk project
(https://github.com/rustdesk/hbb_common), AGPL-3.0; src/gen/ is generated from them.

CHANGES MADE HERE (AGPL section 5(a))
-------------------------------------
- Renamed and re-branded for this project: product name, logo, page title, the
  file name of a saved recording, package name, build output folder.
- "Save password on this device" is switched off: the value it stored (a salted
  hash of the device password) logs in to the device like the password does, and
  this project keeps device credentials out of browser storage. The check box is
  hidden, nothing is saved or loaded, and an earlier saved value is removed.
- The decoder asks for hardware decoding where the browser reports that it has
  it (Chromium), falls back to a browser-chosen decoder if that fails, draws to
  an opaque canvas, and the statistics panel says whether decoding is in
  hardware or software.
- Look: the client's colors are the WebUI's own theme (light and dark, and the six accent colors), chosen by the
  attributes the WebUI's theme.js puts on the page; its former fixed dark palette and orange accent are gone.
- No branding: the top bar has no logo or name, the page title is just "Web client" (the device's ID while connected).
- Icons: the client's hand-drawn icons are replaced by Remix Icon (Apache-2.0, https://remixicon.com) line icons as
  inline SVG, the set the WebUI's menu uses; the client no longer looks for the Remix icon font. The status dot is the
  WebUI's online-badge dot.
- The connect screen is reduced to the device's ID and the password, in the WebUI's sign-in card style, with no top
  bar (the bar appears with the remote screen). The client shows no version and no source text of its own; its
  source, licence and origin are documented in this repository (this folder and the README).
- The bar (which now also shows the stream's numbers), the dock, the chat (a small, resizable window in the bottom
  right corner in place of the Chat and Details side panel) and the menus are redrawn in the WebUI's flat style:
  solid accent, 1px borders, no gradients, no floating island, no avatar, no edge strip.
- The Ctrl, Alt and Del keys and the Keys menu of the dock are replaced by an on-screen keyboard (a movable window
  over the remote screen, new code in input/virtual-keyboard.ts and ui/keyboard-panel.ts): a full US keyboard,
  Ctrl/Shift/Alt/Win as latches (one-shot, or held after a second tap) merged into the modifiers of the keys and
  clicks sent, key repeat, and one-tap shortcuts.
- The file transfer window is redrawn as a two-pane manager over the remote screen: a cursor row and keyboard
  navigation, sortable columns, Send and Receive between the panes, drag and drop from one pane to the other, new
  folder, rename and delete in either pane, and a collapsible queue.
- Build: the output goes into the Python package's static folder, without
  source maps, and with no linked licence files.
- scripts/print-frames.mjs (new): prints the two frames the server's bridge reads,
  as encoded by this client, for the server's tests.

